> limit floor(x)/x x -> 0
limit of floor(x)/x as x -> 0:
  from the left:
  x -> 0 from below
  floor(x)/x -> inf (the numerator -> -1, x -> 0-)
  = inf
  from the right:
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (0)/(1) = lim 0
  = 0
  the one-sided limits differ: the (two-sided) limit does not exist
  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 10, 160, 2560, 40960, 655360, 20971520
    the values grow without bound (+): agrees
  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
    extrapolated (Richardson): 0 (estimated error 0): agrees
